\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Predefined lattices in ALF: (a) square, (b) bilayer square, (c) 3-leg ladder (d) honeycomb and (e) bilayer honeycomb. Nontrivial unit cells are shown as gray regions, while gray sites belong to the second layer in bilayer systems. The links between the orbitals denote the hopping matrix elements and we have assumed, for the purpose of the plot, the absence of hopping in the second layer for bilayer systems. The color coding of the links denotes the checkerboard decomposition. }}{49}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
